===== docs/prompts/implementation-phases/01-reliable-async-maker.md =====
## Documentation requirements

Update in the same change:

- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` for the coordinator, event stream, persistence, and trust boundary;
- `docs/OPENCODE_INTEGRATION.md` for session/event/interrupt behavior and version constraints;
- `docs/OPERATIONS_AND_RECOVERY.md` for restart, reconciliation, cancellation, retention, and unknown outcomes;
- `docs/LOCAL_SETUP.md` for required OpenCode server configuration;
- `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` with completed acceptance evidence and remaining work;
- `docs/DECISIONS.md` for SSE and in-process coordination choices;
- `docs/CHANGELOG.md` and `README.md` for visible Maker behavior.

If a canonical document does not yet exist, create it with only verified and phase-relevant content. Do not update only the old blueprint.

## Acceptance

===== docs/prompts/implementation-phases/02-opencode-onboarding-and-controls.md =====
## Documentation requirements

Update:

- `docs/OPENCODE_INTEGRATION.md` with exact supported version/API surface, credentials ownership, discovery, roles, permissions, sessions, and limitations;
- `docs/LOCAL_SETUP.md` with OpenCode install/start/connect/provider/model steps and troubleshooting;
- `docs/HOSTED_DEPLOYMENT.md` with private-hosted credential handling and public-demo restrictions;
- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` with the configuration and trust boundaries;
- `docs/UX_AND_VISUAL_SYSTEM.md` with onboarding and advanced-control states;
- `docs/DECISIONS.md`, `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`, `docs/CHANGELOG.md`, `.env.example`, and `README.md` as applicable.

Remove obsolete fixed-model statements from active docs while preserving historical records. Never put real credentials in examples.

## Acceptance

===== docs/prompts/implementation-phases/03-workflow-navigation-and-information-architecture.md =====
## Documentation requirements

Update:

- `docs/PRODUCT_BRIEF.md` for the refined user journey and terminology;
- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` for selected-view versus workflow-state ownership;
- `docs/UX_AND_VISUAL_SYSTEM.md` for navigation, section anatomy, states, responsive behavior, and accessibility;
- `docs/OPERATIONS_AND_RECOVERY.md` for stale/blocked state recovery;
- `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`, `docs/DECISIONS.md`, `docs/CHANGELOG.md`, and `README.md`.

Update runtime prompt or schema documentation only where section labels or dependencies actually change. Do not rename the four runtime prompt source files in this phase unless a tested loader migration is included and necessary.

## Acceptance

===== docs/prompts/implementation-phases/04-landing-and-visual-system.md =====
## Documentation requirements

Update:

- `docs/UX_AND_VISUAL_SYSTEM.md` with theme, tokens, component rules, character states, asset prompts/provenance, motion, accessibility, and performance budgets;
- `docs/PRODUCT_BRIEF.md` with positioning and landing claims;
- `docs/LOCAL_SETUP.md` and `docs/HOSTED_DEPLOYMENT.md` so landing instructions match actual setup;
- `docs/DEMO_AND_SUBMISSION.md` with approved screenshots/visual capture guidance;
- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` if asset loading/routes change;
- `docs/DECISIONS.md`, `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`, `docs/CHANGELOG.md`, and `README.md`.

## Acceptance

===== docs/prompts/implementation-phases/05-tool-recommendation-engine.md =====
## Documentation requirements

Update:

- `docs/TOOL_CATALOG.md` with the complete catalog, sources, verification date, classification policy, and maintenance procedure;
- `docs/PRODUCT_BRIEF.md` for user value and recommendation boundaries;
- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` for catalog/rules/model boundaries;
- `docs/UX_AND_VISUAL_SYSTEM.md` for recommendation cards, filters, warnings, and approval states;
- `docs/LOCAL_SETUP.md` for optional local dependencies only when selected;
- `docs/HOSTED_DEPLOYMENT.md` for hosting implications;
- `docs/DECISIONS.md`, `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`, `docs/CHANGELOG.md`, and `README.md`.

Do not place volatile prices only in prose; keep a clearly maintained source/date structure. Do not claim a challenge category without meaningful implemented usage and evidence.

## Acceptance

===== docs/prompts/implementation-phases/06-local-and-hosted-modes.md =====
## Documentation requirements

Update:

- `docs/LOCAL_SETUP.md` with prerequisites, commands, workspace selection, OpenCode connection, troubleshooting, and data locations;
- `docs/HOSTED_DEPLOYMENT.md` with hosted demo versus private Render behavior, costs, secrets, disk, backups, and verification;
- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` with deployment diagrams, capability boundaries, and trust boundaries;
- `docs/OPERATIONS_AND_RECOVERY.md` with mode-specific restart, backup, reset, and incident behavior;
- `docs/PRODUCT_BRIEF.md`, `docs/UX_AND_VISUAL_SYSTEM.md`, `docs/DECISIONS.md`, `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`, `docs/CHANGELOG.md`, `.env.example`, `render.yaml`, and `README.md` as applicable.

Remove obsolete statements that claim only one mode, but preserve historical context in legacy documents until Phase 9.

## Acceptance

===== docs/prompts/implementation-phases/07-deterministic-guided-demo.md =====
## Documentation requirements

Update:

- `docs/DEMO_AND_SUBMISSION.md` with scenario, script, exact claims, fixture provenance, reset behavior, screenshots/video beats, and live-versus-simulated disclosure;
- `docs/PRODUCT_BRIEF.md` with the demo's role in onboarding and judging;
- `docs/UX_AND_VISUAL_SYSTEM.md` with guided-tour behavior and accessibility;
- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` with fixture boundaries and schema reuse;
- `docs/HOSTED_DEPLOYMENT.md` with public demo behavior;
- `docs/OPERATIONS_AND_RECOVERY.md` with reset/isolation behavior;
- `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`, `docs/DECISIONS.md`, `docs/CHANGELOG.md`, and `README.md`.

## Acceptance

===== docs/prompts/implementation-phases/08-backend-and-security-hardening.md =====
## Documentation requirements

Update:

- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` with the final trust-boundary diagram and security ownership;
- `docs/OPERATIONS_AND_RECOVERY.md` with backups, migrations, retention, incidents, failure matrix, budgets, restart, and cleanup;
- `docs/OPENCODE_INTEGRATION.md` with URL/auth/version/retry policies;
- `docs/LOCAL_SETUP.md` and `docs/HOSTED_DEPLOYMENT.md` with secure defaults and troubleshooting;
- `docs/UX_AND_VISUAL_SYSTEM.md` for permission, limit, privacy, and recovery messages;
- `docs/DECISIONS.md`, `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`, `docs/CHANGELOG.md`, `.env.example`, and `README.md`.

Record residual risks honestly, especially shared-host isolation and remote connector deferral.

## Acceptance

===== docs/prompts/implementation-phases/09-release-verification-and-doc-migration.md =====
## Documentation requirements and migration

Make these canonical and accurate:

- `README.md`
- `docs/PRODUCT_BRIEF.md`
- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`
- `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`
- `docs/OPENCODE_INTEGRATION.md`
- `docs/LOCAL_SETUP.md`
- `docs/HOSTED_DEPLOYMENT.md`
- `docs/TOOL_CATALOG.md`
- `docs/UX_AND_VISUAL_SYSTEM.md`
- `docs/OPERATIONS_AND_RECOVERY.md`
- `docs/DEMO_AND_SUBMISSION.md`
- `docs/DECISIONS.md`
- `docs/CHANGELOG.md`

Then:

- Compare legacy documents against canonical content line by line for unique facts and provenance.
- Move genuinely superseded documents into `docs/history/` using Git-aware moves when possible.
- Add a short superseded notice and pointer where stable incoming links may still matter.
- Do not archive the four runtime stage prompts. If they are renamed to clearer names, update loaders, tests, links, provenance, and migration notes atomically:
  - `ORACLE_PRODUCT_DISCOVERY.md`
  - `ARCHITECT_ENGINEERING_PLAN.md`
  - `MAKER_BUILD_AND_VERIFY.md`
  - `WITNESS_DEMO_AND_SUBMISSION.md`
- Keep this implementation prompt pack separate from runtime prompt discovery.
- Remove obsolete active claims, duplicated setup steps, stale model constants, and dead links.
- Add document status/owner/last-verified metadata where it improves maintenance.
- Ensure every user-visible behavior has a setup, operation, recovery, or limitation reference.

## Release and submission handoff

- Prepare a concise release note from the changelog.
- Create an evidence index linking screenshots, demo script, test reports, architecture diagram, OpenCode proof, and selected partner proof.
- Verify challenge/category claims against actual meaningful usage. Do not claim a partner category for installation alone.
- Keep publication, submission, deployment, domain registration, credit claiming, account changes, and public transcript sharing pending unless explicitly authorized.
- Record known limitations and post-release work, especially shared multi-user hosting and remote browser-to-local pairing.

## Acceptance

